    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p><strong>Box&nbsp;6.01</strong> Diagnostic criteria for classic-type myofibroblastoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Breast tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2019. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 2). https://publications.iarc.who.int/581.",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 63.96%; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"63%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histopathology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Purely mesenchymal tumour&nbsp;&ndash; epimyoepithelial components absent</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Well-circumscribed margins; rarely focally infiltrative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Bland-looking, short to elongated spindle cells; minor component: epithelioid to (more rarely) deciduoid-like cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Absent to mild nuclear atypia; nuclear pleomorphism in a minority of cases</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Short, haphazardly intersecting fascicles; focal storiform or neural-like pattern</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Low mitotic count</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Atypical mitoses and necrosis are absent</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Fibrous to myxoid stroma with interspersed thick collagen bundles</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Intratumoural areas of mature adipose tissue can be seen</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Immunohistochemistry&nbsp;/ molecular pathology features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive markers: vimentin, desmin, CD34, ER/PR/AR</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Variable expression of &alpha;-SMA, calponin, CD10, BCL2, CD99</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Negative markers: cytokeratins, EMA, S100, &beta;-catenin, STAT6, RB1, ALK1</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 14; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.36%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"6%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 93.64%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">FISH: 13q14 deletion (in 70&ndash;80% of cases)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 71042,
    "bookid": 84,
    "chapterId": 120,
    "fileId": 48499,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Myofibroblastoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Tumour showing a mostly circumscribed, unencapsulated mass composed of bland spindle to ovoid cells amidst a fibrocollagenous stroma. Mature adipocytes are present within the lesion. Immunohistochemistry shows positive reactivity of the spindle cells for CD34 and desmin.</p>",
    "source": "Imported from 5th edition<br><br><p>SGH Pathology (case contributed by Dr Mihir Gudi)</p>",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/7667.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 71092,
    "bookid": 84,
    "chapterId": 120,
    "fileId": 51061,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Myofibroblastoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Core biopsies of a clinicoradiologically circumscribed breast lump show a spindle cell lesion composed of short spindle fascicles within oedematous and fibrocollagenous stroma. Immunohistochemistry shows CD34, desmin, SMMS, ER and PR positivity, with no staining for AE1/3 and CK7, while Ki67 proliferation is less than 5%.",
    "source": "Tan Puay Hoon",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/51061.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  }
